# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment for the latest version of Qiskit noise learning"
msgstr "Ein Lernexperiment für die neueste Version von Qiskit noise learning erstellen"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment"
msgstr "Ein Lernexperiment erstellen"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment {#build-a-learning-experiment}"
msgstr "Ein Lernexperiment erstellen {#build-a-learning-experiment}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial demonstrates how to build a standard learning experiment from scratch, and use it to learn a model from simulated noisy data.\n"
msgstr "Dieses Tutorial zeigt, wie du ein standardmäßiges Lernexperiment von Grund auf erstellst und damit ein Modell aus simulierten verrauschten Daten lernst.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define a gate set on a ring of qubits\n"
msgstr "Ein Gate-Set auf einem Ring von Qubits definieren\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a 2-local Pauli-Lindblad model\n"
msgstr "Ein 2-lokales Pauli-Lindblad-Modell wählen\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the learning experiment\n"
msgstr "Das Lernexperiment erstellen\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '4.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate circuits\n"
msgstr "Circuits generieren\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '5.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up local simulation\n"
msgstr "Lokale Simulation einrichten\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '6.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the program\n"
msgstr "Das Programm ausführen\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '7.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze the data\n"
msgstr "Die Daten analysieren\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Running on real hardware\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The circuits below are simulated locally, so this walkthrough needs no IBM Quantum® credentials. To alternatively run it on a real device:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Auf echter Hardware ausführen\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Die folgenden Circuits werden lokal simuliert, daher benötigt diese Anleitung keine IBM Quantum®-Zugangsdaten. Um sie stattdessen auf einem echten Gerät auszuführen:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1**: replace [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") with a real backend.\n"
msgstr "**Schritt 1**: Ersetze [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") durch ein echtes Backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  *   **Step 5**: pass that backend as the executor’s mode, and drop the simulator options.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  *   **Schritt 5**: Übergib dieses Backend als Modus des Executors und entferne die Simulatoroptionen.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Define a gate set on a ring of qubits {#1-define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits}"
msgstr "1. Ein Gate-Set auf einem Ring von Qubits definieren {#1-define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a [`QiskitGateSet`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet\") from a backend [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) and a subset of its qubits — here a twelve-qubit ring of [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — then add one gate to it: a layer of six `CZ` gates covering that ring. By default the gate set is initialized with a preparation gate `P` and a measurement gate `M`.\n"
msgstr "Erstelle ein [`QiskitGateSet`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet\") aus dem [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) eines Backends und einer Teilmenge seiner Qubits – hier ein Ring aus zwölf Qubits von [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") – und füge dann ein Gate hinzu: eine Lage aus sechs `CZ`-Gates, die diesen Ring abdeckt. Standardmäßig wird das Gate-Set mit einem Präparations-Gate `P` und einem Mess-Gate `M` initialisiert.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Running on real hardware\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Auf echter Hardware ausführen\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw\") to see the gate on the device topology: the ring of qubits in the gate set, and which pairs of them the gate entangles.\n"
msgstr "Rufe [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw\") auf, um das Gate auf der Gerätetopologie zu sehen: den Ring von Qubits im Gate-Set und welche Paare davon das Gate verschränkt.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Choose a 2-local Pauli-Lindblad model {#2-choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model}"
msgstr "2. Ein 2-lokales Pauli-Lindblad-Modell wählen {#2-choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decide which Pauli-Lindblad generators the noise is allowed to have with a [`PauliLindbladModel`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel\"). Build that generator set from the gate set’s connectivity with [`k_local()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local\") — here every 2-local Pauli on connected qubit pairs of the unitary gate, and single-qubit Paulis for preparation and measurement.\n"
msgstr "Lege mit einem [`PauliLindbladModel`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel\") fest, welche Pauli-Lindblad-Generatoren das Rauschen haben darf. Baue diese Generatormenge mit [`k_local()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local\") aus der Konnektivität des Gate-Sets auf – hier jedes 2-lokale Pauli auf verbundenen Qubit-Paaren des unitären Gates sowie Einzel-Qubit-Paulis für Präparation und Messung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Display the unknown parameter count for the noise model of each gate.\n"
msgstr "Zeige die Anzahl der unbekannten Parameter für das Rauschmodell jedes Gates an.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-learning-experiment\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Build the learning experiment {#3-build-the-learning-experiment}"
msgstr "3. Das Lernexperiment erstellen {#3-build-the-learning-experiment}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble an [`Experiment`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/experiment-builder-experiment#qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment \"qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment\") by composing builder stages. Each stage reads what earlier stages wrote, so order matters:\n"
msgstr "Setze ein [`Experiment`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/experiment-builder-experiment#qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment \"qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment\") aus Builder-Stufen zusammen. Jede Stufe liest, was frühere Stufen geschrieben haben, daher kommt es auf die Reihenfolge an:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observe design matrix rank:\n"
msgstr "Beobachte den Rang der Designmatrix:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"generate-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Generate circuits {#4-generate-circuits}"
msgstr "4. Circuits generieren {#4-generate-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compile the experiment with an [`ExecutorCircuitGenerator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator\"), generating a [`QuantumProgram`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/quantum-program-quantum-program \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — one parameterized template circuit per fragment depth.\n"
msgstr "Kompiliere das Experiment mit einem [`ExecutorCircuitGenerator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator\") und erzeuge dabei ein [`QuantumProgram`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/quantum-program-quantum-program \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") – ein parametrisiertes Template-Circuit pro Fragmenttiefe.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Draw a template circuit to inspect.\n"
msgstr "Zeichne ein Template-Circuit zur Inspektion.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.png](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.png](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"set-up-local-simulation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Set up local simulation {#5-set-up-local-simulation}"
msgstr "5. Lokale Simulation einrichten {#5-set-up-local-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To define the noise model for simulation, we use the generators already in the model with random rates to construct a [`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap).\n"
msgstr "Um das Rauschmodell für die Simulation zu definieren, verwenden wir die bereits im Modell vorhandenen Generatoren mit zufälligen Raten, um eine [`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) zu konstruieren.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Those maps are as wide as the device, since the model is expressed in `backend`’s qubit indexing, but the simulator wants each map to be as wide as the gate it applies to, with Pauli indices running over the gate’s qubits in ascending physical order. Narrow them with [`keep_qubits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap#keep_qubits), which traces out everything off the ring:\n"
msgstr "Diese Maps sind so breit wie das Gerät, da das Modell in der Qubit-Indizierung von `backend` ausgedrückt ist. Der Simulator möchte aber, dass jede Map so breit ist wie das Gate, auf das sie angewendet wird, wobei die Pauli-Indizes in aufsteigender physischer Reihenfolge über die Qubits des Gates laufen. Verschmälere sie mit [`keep_qubits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap#keep_qubits), das alles außerhalb des Rings herausspurt:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulator names a layer’s noise by the box instruction the layer was built from, which [`to_instruction()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction\") returns for any gate in the gate set. Pair each box with its map, use the stabilizer simulation method, and set `seed_simulator` to make the simulated data reproducible:\n"
msgstr "Der Simulator benennt das Rauschen einer Lage nach der Box-Anweisung, aus der die Lage gebaut wurde, die [`to_instruction()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction\") für jedes Gate im Gate-Set zurückgibt. Ordne jede Box ihrer Map zu, verwende die Stabilizer-Simulationsmethode und setze `seed_simulator`, damit die simulierten Daten reproduzierbar sind:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"run-the-program\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Run the program {#6-run-the-program}"
msgstr "6. Das Programm ausführen {#6-run-the-program}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the program, then format the results with [`collect()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect\"), to produce a [`Fit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/analysis-fit#qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit \"qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit\") — the container the analysis stages read from and write to.\n"
msgstr "Führe das Programm aus und formatiere die Ergebnisse dann mit [`collect()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect\"), um ein [`Fit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/analysis-fit#qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit \"qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit\") zu erzeugen – den Container, aus dem die Analysestufen lesen und in den sie schreiben.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This step is the same whether the executor is pointed at a simulator or at a real device.\n"
msgstr "Dieser Schritt ist derselbe, unabhängig davon, ob der Executor auf einen Simulator oder auf ein echtes Gerät zeigt.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"analyze-the-data\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Analyze the data {#7-analyze-the-data}"
msgstr "7. Die Daten analysieren {#7-analyze-the-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build an analysis pipeline around nonnegative least squares fitting of the model.\n"
msgstr "Baue eine Analyse-Pipeline um eine Anpassung des Modells mit nichtnegativen kleinsten Quadraten.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot the measured observable means against their fitted exponentials, one subplot per `CZ` pair, to see whether the decays being fitted are exponential at all.\n"
msgstr "Stelle die gemessenen Mittelwerte der Observablen gegen ihre angepassten Exponentialfunktionen dar, ein Subplot pro `CZ`-Paar, um zu sehen, ob die angepassten Zerfälle überhaupt exponentiell sind.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Swap `exponential_fit` for `model_prediction` to compare the same data against the decays implied by the rates that came out of the non-negative least squares solve.\n"
msgstr "Ersetze `exponential_fit` durch `model_prediction`, um dieselben Daten mit den Zerfällen zu vergleichen, die sich aus den Raten ergeben, die aus der Lösung der nichtnegativen kleinsten Quadrate hervorgegangen sind.\n"
